// Real Ghidra 12.0.4 ground-truth output for a Cortex-M4 freestanding ELF
// whose every public function executes one ARMv7-M synchronization
// instruction (DMB / DSB / ISB / CLREX) or LL/SC primitive (LDREX / STREX).
// Source: firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe.c. Regenerate by running
//
//   cd firmwares/atomics-probe && make
//   bash scripts/ghidra/decompile-headless.sh \
//       --input firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe.elf \
//       --output firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe.json
//   jq . firmwares/atomics-probe/atomics_probe.json \
//       > test/patchir-decomp/callother_atomic_arm_real_ghidra.json
//   (then re-apply this header)
//
// Ghidra emits these CALLOTHER intrinsic targets verbatim: DataMemoryBarrier,
// DataSynchronizationBarrier, InstructionSynchronizationBarrier,
// ClearExclusiveLocal, ExclusiveAccess, hasExclusiveAccess.  The first four
// are normalized by lib/patchestry/AST/IntrinsicHandlers.cpp; the last two
// pass through because they are LL/SC monitor primitives without a clean
// C11 mapping.

